        "passage_id": "P003",
        "quote": "Here, viewing the evidence in the light most favorable to the plaintiffs, as the nonmoving parties, the defendant failed to establish, prima facie, that the injured plaintiff did not know what had caused him to fall. The deposition testimony of the injured plaintiff and his wife, who witnessed the accident, which were submitted in support of the motion, demonstrated the existence of a triable issue of fact as to whether the injured plaintiff tripped and fell as a result of an uneven condition on the second floor landing of the defendant's interior staircase",
